#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106800} :activity/id #uuid "559742f9-a7fb-5d9d-b42f-6e5ba4ec6fe2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050239 :topic/id #uuid "38b346ff-89c2-5572-8fdf-5d288e6ae126" :topic/math-academy-id 1363} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106800 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186107117 :tutorial/content "We can combine stretches in the $x$-direction (with invariant $y$-axis) and stretches in the $y$-direction (with invariant $x$-axis).\n\nFor example, let's consider a combined stretch transformation that performs stretches in the following sequence:\n\n- a stretch in the $x$-direction with stretch factor $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ followed by\n\n- a stretch in the $y$-direction with stretch factor $-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$\n\nThe functional representation of the combined stretch is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}x, -\\dfrac{1}{2}y\\right).\n$$\n\nAs it turns out, it does not matter which stretch we perform first. But it's often helpful to think of the stretches being applied one at a time.\n\nLet's apply our combined stretch transformation to the polygon below.\n\n![](images/9b/9b0338a600efa76b14397a4d60b6de500daf4e136b2233b6fa4f021f0861fc24.png)\n\nTo stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(4,8)$, $(8,-4)$, $(-8,-8)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4,8) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4,\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8)=(2,-4) \\\\ (8,-4) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8,\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4))=(4,2) \\\\ (-8,-8) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-8),\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-8))=(-4,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/ec/ecc35921e58a7a307fe941825209e0009ff7a1bdb42fc252c2b7ef6db7876e75.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "3c0d8bf1-1c0c-5e90-afed-61d70eaa5926" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4725 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "86ae05de-9e43-5780-aadb-91a2390674a1" :step/math-academy-id 29237 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106802}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106801 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105842 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105679 :question/id #uuid "36445a36-7b68-5ba1-847e-7fd720138dd6" :question/math-academy-id "e-7859"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a4270f2-daf1-532d-804a-f293b6f1a8be" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106350} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106532} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534984} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535019}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Polygon"} :step/id #uuid "d8a5d2be-6294-59cf-b218-a7ad2bfec89f" :step/math-academy-id 29238} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106802 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105843 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105680 :question/id #uuid "228d023c-b74d-56a9-ab02-638594472f43" :question/math-academy-id "e-7860"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "043fb5ef-143e-53cc-b83a-15df50446af4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049020}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106351} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106352} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535009} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535074}] :knowledge-point/title "Representing Combined Stretches Using Functions"} :step/id #uuid "1d1ebf4b-bb90-53a4-8143-fdfa9ab8c46c" :step/math-academy-id 29242 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106803}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106803 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105844 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105681 :question/id #uuid "50e74298-c5c0-5bda-bb64-18778f156508" :question/math-academy-id "e-7861"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28d37803-32d2-5b80-aa78-2f0d728e18fe" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106533} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106534} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535028}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Point"} :step/id #uuid "bc9e6b5d-f46